services; and collision repair services comprising fiberglass front and rear cap replacement, windshield replacement, interior remodel solutions, and paint and body work. Further, it offers co-branded credit cards; operates Good Sam Club, a membership organization that offers savings on a range of products and services; and facilitates an RV rental platform that connects travelers with RV owners. The company serves customers through dealerships and service centers, and online and e-commerce platforms. Camping World Holdings, Inc. was founded in 1966 and is headquartered in Lincolnshire, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Matthew D. Wagner | President, CEO & Director | Age 39 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 11K people. Revenue per employee of $572K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers, improving at 7%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Camping World Holdings, Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $474M market cap on $6.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -3% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 17% against a 10% cost of capital, a 7-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 6.6% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 2.7% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (20.6% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 263% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 76% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7629943248356004},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 78/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"What Camping World (CWH) Said on Its Q3 Earnings Call","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/camping-world-cwh-said-q3-041411060.html","date":"2026-11-04","time